2, node3\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"rabbitmqctl cluster_status confirms all three rabbit@node1/2/3 nodes present as Disk Nodes and Running Nodes after join_cluster; reconfirmed identically after each node's restart.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-424928e67bc34e8f\",\"cmd-6812e991a22843a1\",\"cmd-97cbbe7cc6954a1a\",\"cmd-450b01e6c73f42a1\",\"cmd-f9596a20767249d8\",\"cmd-47ddf9670e6446a8\"]},{\"id\":\"req-2\",\"requirement\":\"Serve AMQP over TLS using a certificate authority created for this cluster\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"A dedicated CA (ca-key.pem/ca-cert.pem) was generated on node1 and used to sign per-node server certs and a client cert (openssl verify OK). rabbitmq.conf on each node sets listeners.tcp=none and listeners.ssl.default=5671 with cacertfile/certfile/keyfile pointing at this CA's material; ss -tlnp confirms only 5671/ssl is listening (no plaintext 5672) on all three nodes.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-241b8424102848f5\",\"cmd-5b43628af1034530\",\"cmd-03d6030724a8403f\",\"cmd-0db7e270354d4bb8\",\"cmd-34bb1c7e9da243bc\",\"cmd-2d32d7ce52ed45b0\",\"cmd-067276e28dfe437b\"]},{\"id\":\"req-3\",\"requirement\":\"Accept only client connections presenting a certificate issued by that CA\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"ssl_options.verify=verify_peer and fail_if_no_peer_cert=true are configured on all nodes. Direct TLS tests show: a CA-issued client cert succeeds (Verify return code 0); no client cert triggers a 'certificate required' fatal alert; a cert from a different, untrusted CA triggers a 'Bad Certificate' fatal alert (confirmed both via openssl s_client output and rabbit@node1 log). End-to-end AMQPS publish/consume with the CA-issued client cert succeeded against all three nodes both before and after the restart cycle.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-bdd56213c10c40bb\",\"cmd-aa929addc61e4fb1\",\"cmd-ad123b8e0c51423a\",\"cmd-dceef871b2fd45a0\",\"cmd-fd5f7491bae54d16\",\"cmd-a485c09daecd4652\"]},{\"id\":\"req-4\",\"requirement\":\"Keep the management interface reachable only from within the cluster\",\"status\":\"partially_satisfied\",\"summary\":\"management.tcp.ip binds 15672 to each node's private cluster IP only (not 0.0.0.0), and iptables rules on each node allow 15672 only from the three cluster node IPs followed by a catch-all DROP, persisted via netfilter-persistent. Reachability from within the cluster was verified (401 on bad creds, i.e. connection succeeds). However, no test was captured showing a connection attempt from an IP outside the three-node allowlist was actually blocked/dropped, so the negative case (exclusion of non-cluster sources) rests on configuration inspection rather than an observed blocked connection.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-0db7e270354d4bb8\",\"cmd-34bb1c7e9da243bc\",\"cmd-2d32d7ce52ed45b0\",\"cmd-067276e28dfe437b\",\"cmd-38dbe16d9a134340\",\"cmd-8c7cf7e5ccf14058\",\"cmd-45a6e5a1baa94dfc\",\"cmd-91b4546f2ecd4b52\",\"cmd-51bfbcb3e2764b3a\",\"cmd-63d4b008bdec4ee6\"]},{\"id\":\"req-5\",\"requirement\":\"node1 restart: healthy baseline, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity, and recovered cluster/data/firewall/TLS state\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Pre-reboot boot_id bfd05127... and healthy cluster/queue state captured; reboot issued; connection loss observed across several poll attempts; post-reboot boot_id bf8463cc... (changed) confirmed; rabbitmq-server active, cluster shows 3/3 running, iptables 15672 rules intact, and queue data (tls_test_q) persisted post-restart. Consistent with the fixed lifecycle boot-identity cross-check (bfd05127... -> bf8463cc...).\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-a22783e6ada444a8\",\"cmd-2ed59984cc884b2c\",\"cmd-342c0504f59f4c11\",\"cmd-6f077fc6e0e34256\",\"cmd-a58b727af5454c85\",\"cmd-fac6300f8e5242ce\",\"cmd-450b01e6c73f42a1\"]},{\"id\":\"req-6\",\"requirement\":\"node2 restart: healthy baseline, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity, and recovered cluster/data/firewall/TLS state\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Pre-reboot boot_id cf34dc87... captured; reboot issued with observed connection loss; post-reboot boot_id f499ebdc... confirmed changed; rabbitmq-server active, cluster_status shows 3/3 running, iptables 15672 rules intact. Consistent with fixed lifecycle boot-identity cross-check.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-87d5f9e65eef4eda\",\"cmd-24245756e0934898\",\"cmd-1cba2d4bde1548ed\",\"cmd-f9596a20767249d8\"]},{\"id\":\"req-7\",\"requirement\":\"node3 restart: healthy baseline, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity, and recovered cluster/data/firewall/TLS state\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Pre-reboot boot_id 63f96994... captured; reboot issued with observed connection loss; post-reboot boot_id 1af46fc6... confirmed changed; rabbitmq-server active, cluster_status shows 3/3 running, iptables 15672 rules intact. Consistent with fixed lifecycle boot-identity cross-check. End-to-end AMQPS messaging and TLS client-cert enforcement re-verified against all nodes after the full restart cycle.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-d7431a8f064a4e5b\",\"cmd-84d8085c5924445d\",\"cmd-47bb1c5c107f46cf\",\"cmd-47ddf9670e6446a8\",\"cmd-a485c09daecd4652\"]}],\"confidence\":0.85,\"operational_hygiene\":{\"score\":0.8,\"summary\":\"Most state-changing commands map cleanly to task outcomes: package installs, CA/cert generation, TLS config, cluster join, iptables rules (persisted), user management, and the restart protocol. The temporary HTTP file server used to distribute certs to node2/node3 (cmd-37cd1e1adaf04ab9) was bounded and explicitly torn down afterward (cmd-1c9dc408e96d4d19), which is good practice. One unnecessary mutation was identified: cmd-ff791179a4964a92 wrote an SSH private key to ~/.ssh/id_ed25519 and appended a public key to ~/.ssh/authorized_keys on node1 in an attempt to set up SSH-based file distribution to node2/node3; this attempt failed (return_code 255, sshd inactive on peers) and the executor pivoted to the HTTP-server approach instead. No subsequent command was captured removing the written SSH key material, so this residue (low sensitivity, but an added credential/authorized_keys entry) was not shown to be cleaned up.\",\"evidence_ids\"
